Third-Party Components

This software uses the following third-party components, each distributed under
its own license:

ChronoModel (dating methods, reference curves)

    Website: https://chronomodel.com/
    Source: https://github.com/Chronomodel/chronomodel
    License: GNU General Public License v3.0 or later
    Usage: calibration methods (14C, F14C, Gauss, Unif, TL/OSL, AM) ported to
           src/methods, and the .chr project format

llama.cpp / ggml

    Website: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
    License: MIT License
    Local copy: llama.cpp-LICENSE.txt in the installer, third_party/llama.cpp/LICENSE
    Usage: local inference engine for the language model

QtKeychain

    Website: https://github.com/frankosterfeld/qtkeychain
    License: BSD 2-Clause License
    Local copy: qtkeychain-LICENSE.txt in the installer, third_party/qtkeychain/COPYING
    Usage: storage of the API key in the system keychain

Qt

    Website: https://www.qt.io/
    License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (open source edition)
    License URL: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html
    Usage: application framework (linked dynamically: frameworks on macOS,
           shared libraries on Windows and Linux)

Language model (optional component of the installer)

    Qwen3.5-4B (GGUF quantization), License: Apache License 2.0
    Distributed as a separate data file (models/*.gguf), not linked into SeldonH.
    See LICENCE-modele.txt in the installer.

